From 8c4576572fbce3aa45b10183734387030f8ce9b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:17:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] GBLink JOY Bus: lag model for netplay

A room no longer waits one network trip for every JOY Bus reply. Each machine
runs JoyBusLagModel for a real-GBA port: steady polling is answered with the
real replies of the same cycle one lag (80 ms) ago, the handshaked program
upload is answered from the GBA's acknowledgement pattern, and anything else
waits for the real reply. The GBA itself still gets the game's commands
untouched and on time. Checked against a recorded session (JoyTrace.txt):
134568 commands, 2% waited, the upload predicted exactly but for its last
status. "Netplay lag test" runs the model in solo play.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01764cASb9aVVk2m6JupRMj5
